And that led to them getting divorced.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:26.580
And the divorce courts were not kind to&nbsp;
her at all. She lost everything. She lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:33.360
all of her savings. She got none of it.&nbsp;
She didn't get any partial ownership of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:39.240
the business she had worked her ass off to help&nbsp;
start, and she lost custody of all eight kids.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:48.420
I was, I think, about 13 when that&nbsp;
happened. And I knew she was going to die.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.700
And so I went to live with her.&nbsp;

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:05.160
And it was not a good scene. It was not good&nbsp;
at all. We were actually homeless for a while.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:19.380
So my first day of high school was from a homeless&nbsp;
shelter. And I could go on and on. But the fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

