00:37:03.060 --> 00:37:08.100
down to mitochondria and some people&nbsp;
call it mitochondrial dysfunction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:09.360 --> 00:37:14.220
There's another group of researchers that like&nbsp;
to call it suboptimal mitochondrial function.&nbsp;

00:37:15.300 --> 00:37:17.136
Tim Ferriss: Wouldn't want&nbsp;
to upset those mitochondria.&nbsp;

00:37:17.136 --> 00:37:23.520
Dr. Christopher Palmer: Because that's different&nbsp;
than dysfunction. Yeah, whatever. What it means,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:23.520 --> 00:37:28.440
at the end of the day, and we may get to this,&nbsp;
mitochondria are actually much, much more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:28.440 --> 00:37:34.860
just powerhouses. But powerhouse function is&nbsp;
a critically important function and we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:34.860 --> 00:37:45.420
evidence from numerous data sources, from blood&nbsp;
work, from lumbar punctures, from autopsy studies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:46.380 --> 00:37:51.420
to all of the neuro imaging studies that&nbsp;
we're doing, functional mri, PET scans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:51.420 --> 00:37:59.280
SPECT scans, all of these studies, all of&nbsp;
